# What Cloudflare must not serve. Same syntax as .gitignore, but a completely
# separate mechanism: .gitignore governs what git tracks, and has no bearing on
# what Wrangler uploads once a file exists on disk. Workers static assets
# excludes nothing by default, so without this file the deployment would serve
# .git/config and .git/objects/* at sipi.work.
#
# Anything listed here 404s in production while still passing a local gate, so
# tests/check-load-order.js asserts that no served page references any of it.
# Adding a line the site actually links to fails ./check instead of the site.

.git
.gitignore
wrangler.jsonc
.assetsignore

# Repository tooling. Public in the repository, but not site content, and
# indexing it would only add thin pages to search results.
check
*.py
mutate.js
og-cards.mjs
check-models.js
tests/*.js
tests/*.html
tests/README.md
tests/panels.json

# NOT excluded, deliberately: tests/fixtures/experiments/ and
# tests/fixtures/reference-next/ are linked as downloads from reference.html.

# docs/ is allow-listed rather than deny-listed. The source repository keeps its
# working notes beside the published ledger, and a note that slipped into this
# one should fail closed -- not be served because nobody thought to list it.
# Publishing a new document means adding its line here; a page that links to one
# that is missing fails check-load-order.js, which names it.
docs/*
!docs/absolutes.json
!docs/architecture.md
!docs/channel-model.md
!docs/claims.json
!docs/claims.md
!docs/model-types.json
!docs/pdn-causal-evidence.json
!docs/pdn-causal-model.md
!docs/pdn-two-load-evidence.json
!docs/performance.md
!docs/real-capacitor-model.md
!docs/reference-experiments-next.json
!docs/reference-experiments.json
!docs/reference-experiments.md
!docs/verification-evidence.md

# Files that must never be in this repository at all. Publishing removes them and
# a local pre-push hook refuses any push that still carries one, so in a correct
# deployment each line below matches nothing -- check-load-order.js exempts them
# from its must-match rule, as it does .git. They are here so that if one ever
# got through, Cloudflare still would not serve it.
CLAUDE.md
HANDOVER.md
tests/experimental-labs/*
